{"id": "EUVD-2026-76456", "enisaUuid": "e90fd496-dee7-3797-bd25-387bffd3b23a", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsunrpc: defer rq_argp and rq_resp free until after RCU grace period\n\nsvc_rqst_free() frees rqstp->rq_argp and rqstp->rq_resp synchronously\nvia kfree(), but defers the rqstp struct free via kfree_rcu().  After\nsvc_exit_thread() calls list_del_rcu() and svc_rqst_free(), there is\na window where RCU readers that started before list_del_rcu() can still\ntraverse the thread list and find the rqstp.  These readers (e.g.\nnfsd_nl_rpc_status_get_dumpit()) dereference rqstp->rq_argp, which has\nalready been freed \u2014 a use-after-free.\n\nFix this by moving the kfree of rq_argp and rq_resp into an explicit\ncall_rcu() callback alongside the struct free.  Resources not accessed\nby RCU readers (bvec, buffer pages, scratch folio, auth_data) remain\nsynchronously freed.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:44:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:48:36", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ea49d69aa806008b2424c8cf21cf746b9963967", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/08bc49e0541260bf294962cf889a32a2d2713ad6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0c5693d3f9a5d4911735ab0e0eba4eecb1f1090", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c479bde671cbe2f9e152834a8b0eb7c3c295bbaf"], "aliases": ["GHSA-43p7-fx92-rp4x", "CVE-2026-89545"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0abb1b1b-33c2-3367-bc71-8edac24f70b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3.19"}, {"id": "0bda1819-e95e-33af-8c09-01af7fd9fc6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "51b80146-db6e-3f12-b8cd-9f015ee7cb35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812443865c5fc255363d4a684a62c086af1addca <0ea49d69aa806008b2424c8cf21cf746b9963967"}, {"id": "579196ab-cf03-3ace-8c78-7525b2e5cc6f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "5eafb0e5-dc25-3238-8ff7-0969ec0fee15", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "67ec32b3-ce2e-3554-bc7f-20d468108732", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812443865c5fc255363d4a684a62c086af1addca <e0c5693d3f9a5d4911735ab0e0eba4eecb1f1090"}, {"id": "7b094dba-fc2e-37f7-9328-b9a2a8cf5109", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812443865c5fc255363d4a684a62c086af1addca <c479bde671cbe2f9e152834a8b0eb7c3c295bbaf"}, {"id": "8543419c-22d4-3c50-b156-a6f4b112cdef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "812443865c5fc255363d4a684a62c086af1addca <08bc49e0541260bf294962cf889a32a2d2713ad6"}, {"id": "9309ad30-0f23-3b9e-8fea-93ee2dc09607", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "cfe382a6-213d-36cf-b45b-5b9701b61512", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a6dee0db-9d07-39ff-a8e4-a48379ad87e9", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}